1
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,673
[Grave of Ruan Zheng Feng]

2
00:02:13,274 --> 00:02:15,274
[Episode 10]
[Jealousy Is in the Air]

3
00:02:17,599 --> 00:02:19,240
I wonder

4
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:23,439
if Ms. Dong will even like
these ordinary things.

5
00:02:23,439 --> 00:02:24,960
Pretty funny, don't you think?

6
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:28,600
A second marriage. What's there to celebrate?

7
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,000
Mom, it's getting late. Time to go rest.

8
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,560
I'm heading back.

9
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,720
Back where?

10
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,440
Mingchen Mansion.

11
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,320
What's so great about that place?

12
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:41,520
Can't stand to stay in your home?

13
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,840
Don't move.

14
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:46,480
I didn't.

15
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,960
You say we're even,
but you're still holding a grudge.

16
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,760
Me? Holding a grudge?

17
00:02:56,760 --> 00:03:00,360
Then why are you staring at me like that?

18
00:03:01,148 --> 00:03:03,560
Fine, I'll close my eyes.

19
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:16,580
Done.

20
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,520
Thanks.

21
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,800
Don't mention it.
I should be the one thanking you.

22
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,680
Thank me?

23
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,681
For what?

24
00:03:27,681 --> 00:03:29,760
For what you did for my mentor.

25
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,560
Isn't that what I should have done?

26
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,840
Why thank me for that?

27
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:40,800
Thank you for speaking up for
us employees on the ground from our side.

28
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,680
Eat up.

29
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:03,800
Thanks for the meal.

30
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:08,120
Never thought I'd see the day
the patient cooks for the visitor.

31
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:19,520
This is so delicious.

32
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:23,840
Mr. Fu, you've got some skills.

33
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:25,640
I guess we should thank the noodles.

34
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,360
Try the side dishes.

35
00:04:34,352 --> 00:04:37,040
- Aren't you eating?
- Go ahead. I don't have much of an appetite.

36
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,640
At least have some.

37
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:40,520
I don't like eating alone.

38
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:44,040
Food tastes better when you're sharing it.

39
00:04:50,447 --> 00:04:52,167
Where are you going?

40
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:02,320
- Eat this while it's hot.
- Thank you.

41
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:09,040
It tastes pretty good. Try it.

42
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:20,080
Three-second rule.

43
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,840
Still clean.

44
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:26,720
Didn't peg you as the frugal type.

45
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,200
This way.

46
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,760
Over there.

47
00:06:12,959 --> 00:06:16,520
This place has a certain vibe.

48
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:18,360
But black-and-white photos?

49
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,040
They look so creepy.

50
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,120
Mom, this is the style these days.

51
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:25,120
Just too scary.

52
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:27,720
Bad luck, don't you think?

53
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,200
I knew it.

54
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,480
Look at her, wearing all white again.

55
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,560
Standing there all delicate and demure,

56
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:41,000
making me feel like a peacock all dressed up.

57
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,680
Mom, everyone has their own style.

58
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:47,480
Look, even her lipstick color is so light.

59
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:52,080
And here I am in this attire,
like it's my own wedding anniversary.

60
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,240
Mom, if you don't like Auntie Dong,
just skip the next one she's at.

61
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,560
Can't do that.

62
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:59,880
My gallery needs her.

63
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:04,200
Ms. Dong.

64
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,760
- Mrs. Fu.
- You look so lovely! This dress is gorgeous.

65
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,240
Yours is gorgeous too. So elegant.

66
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,680
Thank you.

67
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,080
Auntie Dong.

68
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:15,370
Ming Yu, I received the necklace you sent.

69
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:17,600
I really love it. You shouldn't have.

70
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,000
He had nothing to do with it.

71
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,760
I was the one who picked it out.

72
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,920
What would a boy know about these things?

73
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,199
Then I should thank you.

74
00:07:25,199 --> 00:07:27,079
You're too kind! I'm glad you like it.

75
00:07:27,079 --> 00:07:28,480
I really love it.

76
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,720
Ms. He!

77
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,240
Ms. He, Ming Yu. You're here!

78
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,241
See?

79
00:07:33,241 --> 00:07:36,840
I told you. It's a small gathering.
Close family friends.

80
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:38,741
This is wonderful.

81
00:07:38,741 --> 00:07:41,600
I haven't seen Fu in ages.

82
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,960
I'm going to steal him for a bit.

83
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,200
"Steal"? Nice.

84
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,440
I know him too well.

85
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:50,560
He'd rather get here early than ride with me.

86
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:52,439
Then you're being unfair to Fu.

87
00:07:52,439 --> 00:07:54,690
Look, you've got him coughing.

88
00:07:54,690 --> 00:07:56,920
I'm telling you, he's not easy to get out.

89
00:07:56,920 --> 00:08:00,079
I've asked him countless times.
Tea, a chat about life...

90
00:08:00,079 --> 00:08:01,120
And he ignores me every time.

91
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:05,360
If it weren't for you, I'd never see him.

92
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,399
Finally got you cornered.

93
00:08:06,399 --> 00:08:08,080
Come on, let's have a talk about life.

94
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,879
- Exactly. Talk about life.
- Look at him.

95
00:08:09,879 --> 00:08:11,280
I'm serious. I do have things to say.

96
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,959
You all go on ahead.

97
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,199
Well, look at them.

98
00:08:15,199 --> 00:08:17,079
Hello, uncles and aunties.

99
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,279
Well, if it isn't Mr. Fu.

100
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:21,000
What brings you here today, Mr. Busy?

101
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,040
Not everyone has as much free time as you.

102
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:25,879
See that? Bickering since they were kids.

103
00:08:25,879 --> 00:08:27,379
You An.

104
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:33,879
Have you said hello to Auntie He?

105
00:08:33,879 --> 00:08:36,039
Hello, Auntie He.

106
00:08:36,039 --> 00:08:37,960
You An, it's been so long.

107
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:41,040
I didn't see you at your mom's last exhibition.

108
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:42,720
What's she been up to?

109
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,600
She just opened a studio.

110
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,360
Been running around nonstop.

111
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,880
If it weren't for this gathering,
we wouldn't have seen her.

112
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:50,159
That's true.

113
00:08:50,159 --> 00:08:52,280
That's how it is when they grow up.

114
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:55,000
Ming Yu's the same.

115
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,640
I barely see him all year.

116
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:00,120
He's about to head to Ma'ao
for a business trip.

117
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,640
How many days this time?

118
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:03,080
You seem to know everything, Mom.

119
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,903
Of course I do.

120
00:09:04,903 --> 00:09:06,840
Ming Yu's going to Ma'ao too??

121
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:09,720
- Yeah, something up?
- Nothing.

122
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:12,240
You An, you mentioned that
you were heading to Ma'ao too.

123
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,200
Said she insisted on going alone.

124
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,559
We couldn't talk her out of it.

125
00:09:15,559 --> 00:09:16,840
That's good.

126
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,920
You see, she's a photographer.

127
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:21,120
She'll be traveling all over the world.

128
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,919
That's wonderful.

129
00:09:22,919 --> 00:09:25,799
But she's a girl, after all.

130
00:09:25,799 --> 00:09:28,519
- We're still a bit worried.
- True.

131
00:09:28,519 --> 00:09:30,000
What's there to worry about?

132
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,480
Ma'ao's easy to get to now.

133
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:35,960
It's easy to get a ride anywhere,
and I've got friends there too.

134
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,559
Don't talk to your mother like that.

135
00:09:37,559 --> 00:09:40,520
She's concerned about you.

136
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:47,279
Ming Yu, how are you getting there?

137
00:09:48,242 --> 00:09:50,120
There's a group going.

138
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:52,760
Probably a business jet?

139
00:09:56,399 --> 00:10:01,799
In that case, Ming Yu,
would you mind taking You An along with you?

140
00:10:01,799 --> 00:10:04,880
It would put our minds at ease.

141
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,400
Would that be too much trouble?

142
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:08,120
Yes, it would.

143
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:10,559
- I'm going for fun, but he's going for work.
- Yes.

144
00:10:10,559 --> 00:10:12,519
I'd cause him trouble.

145
00:10:12,519 --> 00:10:14,279
You two grew up together.

146
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:16,340
She used to chase you around,
calling you "Brother Ming Yu."

147
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:19,120
- Yes, that's right.
- How is that a bother?

148
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:26,799
Listen, while Ming Yu's working,
stay put in the hotel.

149
00:10:26,799 --> 00:10:31,863
And when he's off the clock,
he can keep you company.

150
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:36,760
- Ms. He, Ming Yu, what do you think?
- Look, no...

151
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:38,799
- Uncle Zheng, I don't think--
- It's settled then.

152
00:10:38,799 --> 00:10:43,080
We'll leave all the arrangements
to Ming Yu. Alright?

153
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:46,960
You always have everything so well planned.

154
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:49,240
It's my pleasure.

155
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:52,560
Don't mention it.

156
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:59,080
Fu, could you drop that sour face for once?

157
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,930
You're making Ming Yu nervous.

158
00:11:00,930 --> 00:11:05,480
Everyone else is enjoying themselves,
and he's still buried in work.

159
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:08,600
I get that you want him to succeed.

160
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,960
But back when he was a kid,

161
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:13,000
if he got second place instead of first,
you'd give him a beating.

162
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,480
My son was dead last every time,
and I never did a thing.

163
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:18,406
And look at him now.
Still kicking, doing just fine.

164
00:11:18,406 --> 00:11:20,486
Are you done?

165
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,927
Don't dress up your son's mediocrity
like it's a virtue.

166
00:11:24,927 --> 00:11:27,522
You know, if you had a choice,

167
00:11:27,522 --> 00:11:31,600
would you really trust your entire airline
to Yan An?

168
00:11:32,827 --> 00:11:35,040
Don't even think about it.

169
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:38,240
Why do you have to bring that up?

170
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,559
We're just fundamentally different, you and I.

171
00:11:41,559 --> 00:11:43,800
My philosophy is simple.

172
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,720
We work hard all our lives, but for what?

173
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:50,080
So the next generation
doesn't have to suffer as we did.

174
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,081
Look at Yan An.

175
00:11:51,081 --> 00:11:54,519
He comes around all the time to chat,
to go fishing.

176
00:11:54,519 --> 00:11:55,656
Isn't that nice?

177
00:11:55,656 --> 00:11:57,424
Having him close, enjoying family life.

178
00:11:57,424 --> 00:11:58,679
Now look at you.

179
00:11:58,679 --> 00:12:02,399
If Zheng hadn't organized this,
would you even see your son?

180
00:12:02,399 --> 00:12:06,200
Love it or hate it,
I'm saying this for your own good.

181
00:12:06,788 --> 00:12:10,040
Say, do you always tell your son,
"It's for your own good"?

182
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:12,320
Go away.

183
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,380
Still laughing?

184
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:14,900
Have a drink.

185
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:37,480
[Grave of Ruan Zheng Feng]

186
00:14:28,439 --> 00:14:29,600
Dad.

187
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,520
I'm here to see you.

188
00:14:48,792 --> 00:14:51,113
This is my epaulette.

189
00:14:52,146 --> 00:14:56,146
Three stripes now.

190
00:14:57,519 --> 00:15:02,560
A few more years, and it'll be four.

191
00:15:04,458 --> 00:15:07,699
You know what four stripes mean?

192
00:15:10,085 --> 00:15:14,646
It means I'll be a captain.

193
00:15:21,108 --> 00:15:27,040
It's such a pity
you never got to fly on a plane.

194
00:15:29,519 --> 00:15:32,479
If you could've held on just a little longer,

195
00:15:33,711 --> 00:15:38,840
maybe you could've sat in a plane I was flying.

196
00:15:39,606 --> 00:15:41,887
I could've taken you abroad.

197
00:15:44,885 --> 00:15:49,880
The wind's been really strong
these past few nights.

198
00:15:51,068 --> 00:15:56,640
It was howling outside the window.

199
00:15:56,640 --> 00:16:02,560
I was half-asleep, and for a moment,
I thought I was back in our old house.

200
00:16:08,265 --> 00:16:14,251
Xiao Zhen always says
my new apartment is so upscale,

201
00:16:15,039 --> 00:16:18,073
but honestly, I don't think
it holds a candle to our home.

202
00:16:18,073 --> 00:16:20,466
Besides,

203
00:16:20,466 --> 00:16:23,640
a guy is living upstairs who's really annoying.

204
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:34,440
Well, "annoying" isn't entirely fair.

205
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:39,041
After all, he has his moments, good and bad.

206
00:16:41,759 --> 00:16:44,880
What am I even going on about?

207
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,840
Dad,

208
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:50,240
just forget what I just said.

209
00:16:54,893 --> 00:16:56,933
Let me...

210
00:16:58,513 --> 00:17:01,113
stay here quietly with you for a while.

211
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:23,800
[Jiang City]

212
00:17:24,993 --> 00:17:28,439
Ruan, why walking so fast?

213
00:17:28,439 --> 00:17:29,600
Out of breath?

214
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,840
Why so slow?

215
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:32,440
Hurry up.

216
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:19,439
[Yellow Alert: Thunderstorms and Strong Winds]

217
00:18:19,439 --> 00:18:21,240
So, how are things with you lately?

218
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:23,120
Don't even ask.

219
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:25,760
Is it true he said you're too tall?

220
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,560
But I'm not even wearing heels.

221
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:29,360
Neither am I.

222
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:31,000
Exactly.

223
00:18:39,886 --> 00:18:41,806
<i>Remember to bring an umbrella.</i>

224
00:18:50,663 --> 00:18:53,679
<i>Mr. Fu, out with your girlfriend
and still checking in on me?</i>

225
00:18:53,679 --> 00:18:55,693
<i>Isn't that a little inappropriate?</i>

226
00:18:55,693 --> 00:18:57,653
Girlfriend?

227
00:19:18,799 --> 00:19:21,319
<i>She's not my girlfriend.</i>

228
00:19:26,199 --> 00:19:29,880
Mr. Fu, would you like some yogurt?

229
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:32,960
No thanks. Too sour.

230
00:19:33,959 --> 00:19:35,679
You An, you want some?

231
00:19:35,679 --> 00:19:39,560
No? Guess I'll have it myself.

232
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,320
Yeah, pretty sour.

233
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:47,199
Excuse me, sir. We're about to take off.

234
00:19:47,199 --> 00:19:50,159
Please turn off your electronic devices.

235
00:19:50,159 --> 00:19:53,320
Mr. Yang, we have water, coffee,
and other soft drinks available.

236
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:55,040
What would you like?

237
00:19:55,040 --> 00:19:56,600
- Water, please.
- Thank you.

238
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:59,360
- Ma'am, please fasten your seat belt.
- Thank you.

239
00:20:01,399 --> 00:20:04,040
Sir, please put your seatback
in the upright position.

240
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:22,720
<i>Why aren't you replying?</i>

241
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:52,240
[Ma'ao]

242
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:53,880
Yan An, I'm warning you.

243
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:56,679
Get in front of me right now.

244
00:20:56,679 --> 00:20:58,560
Or you'd better hope luck's on your side today.

245
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:01,680
Because if not,
I'll show you who's really in charge.

246
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,120
Right here!

247
00:21:06,199 --> 00:21:07,520
What's all this?

248
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:09,280
Scored some free milk tea.

249
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:13,719
The heir of Bo'ao is wooing me with freebies?

250
00:21:13,719 --> 00:21:16,520
When it comes to money,
save where you can, spend where you must.

251
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:18,639
And the whole point of me saving

252
00:21:18,639 --> 00:21:21,560
is so I can dedicate the rest of the day
to you.

253
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:23,960
You can do whatever you want.

254
00:21:25,679 --> 00:21:27,120
Sweet enough?

255
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:29,560
I need a dopamine hit right now.

256
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:30,880
Then you need me.

257
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:32,056
Let's go.

258
00:21:32,056 --> 00:21:35,360
Come on, take this. Let's go.

259
00:21:37,318 --> 00:21:38,800
Go.

260
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:47,960
Oh no, I want to try every flavor.

261
00:21:49,924 --> 00:21:52,840
I'm not trying to be cheap,
but we've got a long food tour ahead.

262
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,760
Don't fill up on ice cream.

263
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:56,800
Then I can't pick.

264
00:21:58,679 --> 00:22:01,840
Alright, pick your top two favorites.

265
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:04,840
Whatever you don't finish,
I'll take care of it.

266
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:08,679
Max three, I'm serious.

267
00:22:08,679 --> 00:22:11,399
Think about it.
If you grab four and take one bite of each,

268
00:22:11,399 --> 00:22:13,560
how can I finish all the rest?

269
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:15,160
Deal!

270
00:22:15,846 --> 00:22:18,646
I'll take chocolate, honeydew...

271
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:22,560
And lemon, please.

272
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,760
Thanks!

273
00:22:30,115 --> 00:22:32,120
Not bad. You've got good taste.

274
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:33,560
Of course.

275
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:37,999
Every time I land in Ma'ao,
this is my first stop.

276
00:22:37,999 --> 00:22:39,200
Save some room.

277
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:41,440
There's way more good stuff coming.

278
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:42,727
You actually planned this out?

279
00:22:42,727 --> 00:22:44,399
I don't need a plan for this place.

280
00:22:44,399 --> 00:22:45,639
Who are you looking down on?

281
00:22:45,639 --> 00:22:47,200
Let's roll.

282
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:54,560
Keep showing off.

283
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:18,320
Long time no see, Uncle Cai!

284
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:19,639
Hey, handsome!

285
00:24:19,639 --> 00:24:21,720
Haven't seen you in forever.

286
00:24:23,239 --> 00:24:26,159
Finally got yourself a girlfriend?

287
00:24:26,159 --> 00:24:29,080
Don't start. She's a friend.
Known her since we were kids.

288
00:24:29,080 --> 00:24:32,999
So, childhood sweethearts!

289
00:24:32,999 --> 00:24:34,639
You're chatty today.

290
00:24:34,639 --> 00:24:38,080
- Two bowls, extra tripe and offal.
- All right, all right.

291
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:39,679
On the house.

292
00:24:39,679 --> 00:24:41,679
Just save me a seat at your wedding!

293
00:24:41,679 --> 00:24:43,159
You'll definitely be invited.

294
00:24:43,159 --> 00:24:44,600
But I'm paying. Here you go.

295
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:46,800
- Here, yours.
- Seriously? This much?

296
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:48,760
How am I supposed to
eat anything else after this?

297
00:24:48,760 --> 00:24:49,800
We'll get going then.

298
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:50,840
Thank you.

299
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:53,280
- Bye-bye.
- Bye.

300
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:55,679
What's the matter?

301
00:24:55,679 --> 00:24:56,880
I'm fine.

302
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:58,680
Period.

303
00:25:01,440 --> 00:25:04,080
[She's not my girlfriend.]
[Why aren't you replying?]

304
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:05,680
Ruan.

305
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:07,719
Have some warm water.

306
00:25:07,719 --> 00:25:09,840
- Be careful, it's hot.
- Thank you.

307
00:25:09,840 --> 00:25:11,880
I saw you weren't feeling well earlier.

308
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:14,280
Want me to call you a taxi?

309
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:15,526
I'm fine.

310
00:25:15,526 --> 00:25:17,239
I'm going to Mingchen Mansion today.

311
00:25:17,239 --> 00:25:19,400
My friend lives there.

312
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:23,720
Come with me.

313
00:25:26,999 --> 00:25:28,800
Nice shot!

314
00:25:48,679 --> 00:25:50,360
You An?

315
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:56,080
You An?

316
00:25:57,679 --> 00:25:59,800
You An, you okay?

317
00:26:01,080 --> 00:26:03,040
I'm coming in.

318
00:26:04,439 --> 00:26:06,200
You An.

319
00:26:07,199 --> 00:26:09,520
You An, what happened?

320
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:11,720
Get up.

321
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:12,919
Where does it hurt?

322
00:26:12,919 --> 00:26:15,040
- My belly hurts.
- Your belly?

323
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:17,080
Come, get back to bed.

324
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:18,580
Come on.

325
00:26:21,199 --> 00:26:22,840
Careful.

326
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:25,760
Hang in there. I'll call a doctor.

327
00:26:28,337 --> 00:26:30,520
Hello? I need a doctor right now.

328
00:26:30,520 --> 00:26:33,080
Send one up to my room. Hurry, please!

329
00:26:36,520 --> 00:26:38,520
Let me get you some water.

330
00:26:39,760 --> 00:26:41,600
Here, want some?

331
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,720
- No.
- All right.

332
00:26:45,053 --> 00:26:46,439
Just hold on. I told the front desk.

333
00:26:46,439 --> 00:26:48,440
The doctor will be here soon.

334
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:50,439
I'm right here with you.

335
00:26:50,439 --> 00:26:52,320
Don't be scared.

336
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:53,840
If it hurts, just let it out.

337
00:26:53,840 --> 00:26:55,760
I'm right here.

338
00:27:01,270 --> 00:27:03,320
You went back home?

339
00:27:03,320 --> 00:27:05,239
Then you...

340
00:27:05,239 --> 00:27:06,320
All right.

341
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:08,480
Never mind, I'm fine.

342
00:27:09,166 --> 00:27:11,406
You go ahead.

343
00:27:15,999 --> 00:27:19,120
I'll grab a taxi. Thanks anyway.

344
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:20,719
Come to my place.

345
00:27:20,719 --> 00:27:22,239
It's just upstairs.

346
00:27:22,239 --> 00:27:24,080
I don't want to trouble you.

347
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:26,920
Alright, you're going back on your own?

348
00:27:29,816 --> 00:27:31,999
Your skirt is stained.

349
00:27:31,999 --> 00:27:33,399
Where?

350
00:27:33,399 --> 00:27:35,439
How bad is it? Is it noticeable?

351
00:27:35,439 --> 00:27:37,160
This much.

352
00:27:41,399 --> 00:27:44,720
Then can I go to your place to wash my skirt?

353
00:27:56,178 --> 00:27:57,219
Just lie down.

354
00:27:57,219 --> 00:27:58,579
I have some brown sugar.

355
00:27:58,579 --> 00:28:00,679
- I'll brew some for you.
- Thank you.

356
00:28:00,679 --> 00:28:03,400
I'm never drinking cold drinks again.

357
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:27,280
[She's not my girlfriend.]
[Why aren't you replying?]

358
00:28:28,084 --> 00:28:30,384
Why are you telling me this?

359
00:28:30,384 --> 00:28:33,440
Like you're explaining yourself to me.

360
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:37,640
[Got it.]

361
00:28:46,366 --> 00:28:48,806
<i>Busy. Didn't see it.</i>

362
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:57,400
<i>Ignoring messages is rude.</i>

363
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:03,600
<i>First day knowing me?</i>

364
00:29:03,600 --> 00:29:08,600
<i>I'm not rude, but I choose not to be polite.</i>

365
00:29:18,076 --> 00:29:19,959
<i>Ruan Si Xian, don't push your luck.</i>

366
00:29:19,959 --> 00:29:22,640
<i>I don't have endless patience for you.</i>

367
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:24,040
<i>Is it because of Zheng You An?</i>

368
00:29:24,040 --> 00:29:26,160
<i>Are you jealous?</i>

369
00:29:39,840 --> 00:29:42,840
Mr. Fu, are you that free? Aren't you tired?

370
00:29:42,840 --> 00:29:43,919
No work? No meetings?

371
00:29:43,919 --> 00:29:46,240
Don't you need to rest at this hour?

372
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:54,600
Ruan, I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

373
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:56,920
I just came out to use the bathroom.

374
00:30:04,738 --> 00:30:09,000
But you can't talk to him like that.

375
00:30:09,635 --> 00:30:13,760
- Why not?
- If you do, it'll backfire.

376
00:30:13,760 --> 00:30:16,320
You need to know how to handle it.

377
00:30:21,919 --> 00:30:25,080
<i>Since you know I'm busy, keep it down.</i>

378
00:30:25,080 --> 00:30:26,679
<i>I'll be back next Saturday.</i>

379
00:30:26,679 --> 00:30:28,999
So what if you're coming back? Why tell me?

380
00:30:28,999 --> 00:30:33,600
What, want me to roll out a red carpet
and grab a megaphone to welcome you?

381
00:30:54,600 --> 00:30:57,025
What did you say?

382
00:30:57,025 --> 00:31:00,485
That's not the way to show concern.

383
00:31:00,485 --> 00:31:02,367
You have to take it step by step.

384
00:31:02,367 --> 00:31:05,080
If you bombard him with questions like that,
he'll get annoyed.

385
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:06,239
Why would I care about him?

386
00:31:06,239 --> 00:31:10,360
Am I supposed to check if his brain
needs an upgrade or a reboot?

387
00:31:10,360 --> 00:31:13,760
I'm trying to give you some advice.

388
00:31:13,760 --> 00:31:16,160
No need to snap at me.

389
00:31:21,362 --> 00:31:22,790
Drink this.

390
00:31:22,790 --> 00:31:24,439
I don't want that.

391
00:31:24,439 --> 00:31:26,479
Fine, don't then.

392
00:31:26,479 --> 00:31:28,535
I'm never crossing you again.

393
00:31:28,535 --> 00:31:31,560
You're fierce enough to fight with your boss,

394
00:31:31,560 --> 00:31:33,439
and I definitely couldn't take you either.

395
00:31:33,439 --> 00:31:37,680
I heard your fitness test scores are insane.

396
00:31:51,919 --> 00:31:53,560
Drink it.

397
00:32:11,879 --> 00:32:13,639
Come on in.

398
00:32:17,867 --> 00:32:19,840
Welcome to my humble abode.

399
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:22,774
Humble? Are you serious?

400
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:25,280
Make yourself at home. I'll be right back.

401
00:32:35,397 --> 00:32:37,560
Why don't you take a hot shower?

402
00:32:37,560 --> 00:32:39,399
Don't want you catching a cold.

403
00:32:39,399 --> 00:32:41,840
Thanks.

404
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:43,640
Give me your clothes.

405
00:32:44,959 --> 00:32:46,680
Where's the...

406
00:32:46,680 --> 00:32:48,199
Bathroom's in there.

407
00:32:48,199 --> 00:32:49,960
Thanks.

408
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:55,280
The T-shirt is new.

409
00:32:55,280 --> 00:32:57,160
Got it.

410
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:09,080
This is to prevent a cold.

411
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:12,040
- Careful, it's hot.
- Thank you.

412
00:33:12,040 --> 00:33:13,680
Let me.

413
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:33,399
What are you grinning about?

414
00:33:33,399 --> 00:33:34,639
Nothing.

415
00:33:34,639 --> 00:33:39,360
Just feels like I won the lottery or something.

416
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:42,760
Commander Zhen,

417
00:33:42,760 --> 00:33:46,160
a little luck is fine,
but too much and you might get burned.

418
00:33:58,317 --> 00:34:01,685
You read Gao Mu's "Alone" series too?

419
00:34:01,685 --> 00:34:03,440
I have the whole set.

420
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:05,600
I think she's adorable.

421
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:07,520
I think you're adorable too.

422
00:34:10,119 --> 00:34:12,392
You're too kind.

423
00:34:12,392 --> 00:34:15,760
I always thought I'd end up alone,

424
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:19,680
just like Gao Mu.

425
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:02,080
There, all done.

426
00:35:03,919 --> 00:35:06,760
Thank you.

427
00:35:11,119 --> 00:35:13,320
Come with me.

428
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:14,960
What for?

429
00:35:15,599 --> 00:35:18,440
What is it? Why so mysterious?

430
00:35:23,718 --> 00:35:24,840
Oh my gosh!

431
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:27,766
You have all of these!

432
00:35:27,766 --> 00:35:30,440
All of them are the latest editions.

433
00:35:30,440 --> 00:35:33,640
Oh my gosh, this is heaven!

434
00:35:33,640 --> 00:35:35,160
And you have these too?

435
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:37,040
I've never had anyone
to talk to about this stuff.

436
00:35:37,040 --> 00:35:39,565
I love these so much.

437
00:35:39,565 --> 00:35:41,479
Can I open it and have a closer look?

438
00:35:41,479 --> 00:35:43,080
Sure.

439
00:35:46,559 --> 00:35:49,800
Oh my gosh, these are all authentic!

440
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:51,626
Can't be bootlegs, right?

441
00:35:51,626 --> 00:35:53,399
I could only read bootlegs back then.

442
00:35:53,399 --> 00:35:56,240
Some of them were
even passed around the whole class.

443
00:35:57,708 --> 00:35:59,928
I see. I'll send you my door code.

444
00:35:59,928 --> 00:36:02,880
Anytime you want to read, just come over.

445
00:36:02,880 --> 00:36:05,160
- Really?
- Really.

446
00:36:10,959 --> 00:36:15,679
Then I'm borrowing these for now.

447
00:36:15,679 --> 00:36:17,440
Okay.

448
00:36:47,519 --> 00:36:48,880
Your hand gets cold during a drip.

449
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:51,000
But I'll keep it warm like this.
You can sleep better,

450
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:53,160
and your hand won't move around.

451
00:37:26,388 --> 00:37:28,061
You An.

452
00:37:28,061 --> 00:37:29,119
Bai Yang.

453
00:37:29,119 --> 00:37:30,840
Feeling any better?

454
00:37:31,757 --> 00:37:34,076
Mr. Fu had me bring you breakfast.

455
00:37:34,076 --> 00:37:35,237
Very light.

456
00:37:35,237 --> 00:37:39,210
The doctor will check on you,
and you can eat if everything is okay.

457
00:37:39,210 --> 00:37:40,790
Fu Ming Yu came by?

458
00:37:40,790 --> 00:37:44,119
Yes, he came right over
after Mr. Yan called him last night.

459
00:37:44,119 --> 00:37:46,039
But he went to a meeting this morning.

460
00:37:46,039 --> 00:37:48,299
I'll be here to look after you both.

461
00:37:48,299 --> 00:37:49,960
Call me if you need anything.

462
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:51,760
I'll be right outside the door.

463
00:37:52,559 --> 00:37:54,360
Get some rest.

464
00:38:13,480 --> 00:38:16,280
Mom, Unit One at Mingchen Mansion.

465
00:38:16,280 --> 00:38:18,120
Are you here?

466
00:38:18,120 --> 00:38:20,800
Okay, I'll be right down.

467
00:38:24,327 --> 00:38:27,039
Ruan, I'm feeling much better.

468
00:38:27,039 --> 00:38:28,640
Want me to walk you down?

469
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:32,040
No, it's fine. My mom's picking me up.

470
00:38:33,345 --> 00:38:34,826
Thanks for yesterday.

471
00:38:34,826 --> 00:38:36,506
Don't mention it.

472
00:38:46,360 --> 00:38:47,559
Ruan.

473
00:38:47,559 --> 00:38:51,360
Well, when it comes to going after someone,
you need to have a plan,

474
00:38:51,360 --> 00:38:53,399
- especially with--
- What?

475
00:38:53,399 --> 00:38:54,960
Especially with a guy like Mr. Fu--

476
00:38:54,960 --> 00:38:56,999
Isn't your mom waiting for you downstairs?

477
00:38:56,999 --> 00:38:58,680
An adult still needs her mom to pick her up?

478
00:38:58,680 --> 00:39:01,080
You're grown enough to be a mom yourself.

479
00:39:04,992 --> 00:39:06,912
I'm leaving.

480
00:39:13,245 --> 00:39:16,119
Mind your own business.
I'll always be my mom's little girl!

481
00:39:16,119 --> 00:39:17,720
<i>Mom!</i>

482
00:39:18,399 --> 00:39:21,200
<i>- Feeling better?
- Yeah, much better.</i>

483
00:39:26,240 --> 00:39:27,800
<i>I had some brown sugar water.</i>

484
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:31,720
<i>Good. I'll make you ginger brown sugar water
and braised pork back home.</i>

485
00:39:31,720 --> 00:39:34,240
<i>I want the braised pork, Mom!</i>

486
00:39:50,538 --> 00:39:53,019
<i>Silk scarf designed by Mom.</i>

487
00:40:05,439 --> 00:40:08,959
<i>That unreliable guy
can be this thoughtful sometimes.</i>

488
00:40:08,959 --> 00:40:11,200
<i>Sorry for the trouble, everyone.</i>

489
00:40:16,959 --> 00:40:19,240
Isn't that Bai Yang?

490
00:40:22,634 --> 00:40:28,040
Not your girlfriend,
but you let her take your plane?

491
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:32,640
Not your girlfriend, but you take her to Ma'ao
and hold her hand all night?

492
00:40:35,035 --> 00:40:37,479
Scumbag.

493
00:40:37,479 --> 00:40:40,200
So, where are you going next?

494
00:40:40,200 --> 00:40:42,880
I'm going to Miami to attend a meeting.

495
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:45,519
- When are you leaving?
- Tomorrow.

496
00:40:45,519 --> 00:40:46,599
Thank you, sir.

497
00:40:46,599 --> 00:40:47,840
Okay, all the best.

498
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:49,360
Okay, see you next time.

499
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:51,600
- See you.
- Have a good trip.

500
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:03,119
Babe...

501
00:41:03,119 --> 00:41:04,200
well...

502
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:05,800
Yes, I know I missed your calls.

503
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:09,479
I've been stuck in meetings
with Mr. Fu all day.

504
00:41:09,479 --> 00:41:11,360
[The sherry here is pretty good.]
Yeah, just wrapped up, just stepped out,

505
00:41:11,360 --> 00:41:12,760
just saw your calls.

506
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:14,760
Are you going to bed? Okay, get some sleep.

507
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:16,160
Good.

508
00:41:16,160 --> 00:41:17,920
Have fun.

509
00:41:20,787 --> 00:41:22,334
Sorry about that, Mr. Fu.

510
00:41:22,334 --> 00:41:24,399
Well...

511
00:41:24,399 --> 00:41:26,479
If I don't check in, I get an earful.

512
00:41:26,479 --> 00:41:28,399
If I check in too much, I'm annoying.

513
00:41:28,399 --> 00:41:31,280
Simply put: Hard.

514
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:34,800
Too much contact gets annoying?

515
00:41:34,800 --> 00:41:36,599
Of course it does.

516
00:41:36,599 --> 00:41:38,439
Either I don't reach out enough,

517
00:41:38,439 --> 00:41:40,519
or I'm texting her nonstop.

518
00:41:40,519 --> 00:41:43,486
In the world of romance,
it's all about two words:

519
00:41:43,486 --> 00:41:46,006
"Balance."

520
00:41:47,820 --> 00:41:50,029
That's one word.

521
00:41:50,029 --> 00:41:51,869
Right, one word.

522
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:55,600
So yours is like that too.

523
00:41:56,439 --> 00:41:58,157
Never mind. What day is it today?

524
00:41:58,157 --> 00:41:59,605
Wednesday.

525
00:41:59,605 --> 00:42:01,319
Right.

526
00:42:01,319 --> 00:42:03,079
Okay.

527
00:42:11,119 --> 00:42:13,479
There's one thing
to pay special attention to today.

528
00:42:13,479 --> 00:42:15,840
About 15 minutes after takeoff
on our return flight,

529
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:18,119
we'll encounter a thunderstorm area.

530
00:42:18,119 --> 00:42:21,640
Our priority is to
notify the cabin crew immediately...

531
00:42:41,150 --> 00:42:43,039
Flying requires reverence.

532
00:42:43,039 --> 00:42:47,160
Reverence for life, for duty,
and for the rules.

533
00:42:57,512 --> 00:42:59,793
It's already three o'clock.

534
00:43:00,739 --> 00:43:02,899
Saturday...

535
00:43:03,747 --> 00:43:07,747
I feel like someone mentioned Saturday to me.

536
00:43:08,945 --> 00:43:10,504
Ruan.

537
00:43:11,177 --> 00:43:13,360
Mr. Bai.

538
00:43:13,360 --> 00:43:15,720
Mr. Fu would like to see you in his office.

539
00:43:15,720 --> 00:43:17,720
Me?

540
00:43:18,600 --> 00:43:19,680
For what?

541
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:20,785
Nothing specific, I think.

542
00:43:20,785 --> 00:43:22,065
He just asked you to come over.

543
00:43:22,065 --> 00:43:23,706
Let's go.

544
00:43:27,720 --> 00:43:30,720
What is he up to now?

545
00:43:40,365 --> 00:43:41,485
I have another meeting.

546
00:43:41,485 --> 00:43:43,166
It might take a while.

